{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SaEiga3LkuCdsmjGdGzUGk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty**, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **markdown files as the source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing, Python stdlib only (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n\n- **Ships a local web-app dashboard** (`anchor_gui.py`) â€” a self-contained stdlib HTTP server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It reads/writes the markdown task files directly and regenerates the full dashboard HTML on every request.\n\n- **Core function = task & project management**: tasks move through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-later â†’ Restored) across a daily dashboard, an inbox, and per-domain files (`domains/academic.md`, `commercial.md`, `family.md`, `writing.md`). A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) does the same and emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Has grown a major second surface â€” an R&D \"Project Cockpit\"** for managing AI \"trio\" work (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Each project gets a window where lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) appear as **status-lit tiles**; clicking expands an **inline panel with a cached summary over a real, resizable terminal**.\n\n- **The terminal substrate is real ConPTY** (via `pywinpty` + xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport), with **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a durable session registry, engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), stage handoffs, cached/validated project & session summaries, and a port-â‰ 8777-guarded deliverable preview runner.\n\n- **Self-verifying**: a daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every file and exercises every endpoint plus the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed, writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"** The R&D surface has shipped through **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built by Foreman, merged to master 2026-06-13; revision v4.1 rebuilt the project-window render clean against the mockup).\n\nThe latest commits confirm active work on making the cockpit's project-window render match its design (v4.1, \"Cockpit render for real\") with a visible build stamp to tell deployed-vs-cached apart."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbb8c660-d203-4539-b1d4-cea3eaa1b033","uuid":"e614dc40-51e3-4fa6-a805-6b189b9c7922","request_id":"req_011Cc2MfRMKF3DHiSKVhNQfc"}
